00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:18.740
What is it?

148
00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:24.060
Yeah, it's an independent commissioner who has several other people to help investigate

149
00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.380
complaints regarding health care.

150
00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:32.820
So technically the commissioner is one person, but it sort of speaks on others who work on

151
00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:33.820
her behalf also.

152
00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:34.820
Yeah.

153
00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:35.820
Okay.

154
00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:36.820
Okay.

155
00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:37.820
And what's the purpose of the commissioner?

156
00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:42.460
So everybody using a health or disability service have rights.

157
00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:48.020
So there's a code of rights and it's there to promote these rights and also protect consumers

158
00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:52.860
to make sure everyone is treated fairly and correctly when using health services.

159
00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:58.540
So what sort of practices and services does the HDC, as we'll pull it from here, what

160
00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:01.380
does, what does they have oversight over?

161
00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:02.380
A whole bunch.

162
00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:10.020
So you've got through to like age, residential care, to hospitals, to dentists, dental assistants,

163
00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.020
pharmacists.

164
00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:15.460
So a whole huge umbrella of people under health services.

165
00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:20.980
So it can be organisations, it can be individual practitioners, does it include like naturopaths

166
00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:24.180
and sort of alternative, you know, practitioners?

167
00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.180
Yeah.

168
00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.180
And what about councillors?

169
00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:27.180
Yeah.

170
00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:31.380
I'm guessing, because disability is in the name of the Health and Disability Commissioner

